  title `The Central Sales Tax Act, 1956`
  localizedTitles obj_root_laws_the_central_sales_tax_act_1956_localized_titles
  actNumber (74)
  actYear (1956)
  enactmentDate 1956-10-21
  ministry `Ministry of Finance`
  department `Department of Revenue`
  longTitle `An Act to formulate principles for determining when a sale or purchase of goods takes place in the course of inter-State trade or commerce or outside a State or in the course of import into or export from India, to provide for the levy, collection and distribution of taxes on sales of goods in the course of inter-State trade or commerce and to declare certain goods to be of special importance in inter-State trade or commerce and specify the restrictions and conditions to which State laws imposing taxes on the sale or purchase of such goods of special importance shall be subject.`
